{
  "_about": "Look pack drafts, one per studied style (styles/<note>.md). A look is tokens and motion defaults a video repo starts from; it never copies a creator's material. Keys are the same for every look so an agent can diff two and so the kit can read one into theme.css and look.json (roadmap VP-6). Sizes are pixels on a 1920x1080 stage; times in milliseconds unless the key says seconds; every value must clear craft/rules.json (text floors 72/72/54 px, 42 characters, accent share 0.10, still run 8 s full and 12 s formal). 'after' credits the style studied; 'pacing' is the creator's measured rate and our target, so the gap is visible. Drafted 30 Sep 2026; nothing here is built in the kit yet.",
  "keys": {
    "ground": "stage background",
    "ink": "text and stroke colour on that ground",
    "paper": "the surface of a card, clipping or slide when it differs from the ground",
    "accents": "at most three, in priority order; the checker sums their share",
    "type": "family class, weight, case and the sizes used for title, label and body",
    "strokes": "width in px, seeded roughness 0 to 1, glow in px, cap style",
    "entrance": "how an element arrives: kind, duration ms, easing, distance px or scale from",
    "camera": "static, push, or drift; percent of frame height per second; scale change over a hold",
    "cutSeconds": "seconds between shots, full and formal",
    "holdSeconds": "longest still without a build or a moving camera, full and formal",
    "textOnFrame": "what kinds of text appear: none, labels, bullets, titles, code, captions",
    "evidence": "what shows a fact: recreated screens, documents, icons, figures",
    "sceneKinds": "the rig's scene kinds this look serves best",
    "pacing": "words per minute: creator measured, our target; sentence average words",
    "voice": "the register the narration takes in this look, in a phrase"
  },
